A /model pick under Pi also persists as Grok's global default_model, and a failed switch doesn't roll back the persisted value (OBSERVATIONS.md, gb-tui-controls section). Decide: scope default_model per agent, or don't persist on external-agent switches.
Once in a claude run a stray `/resume-claude <id>` prompt was sent at startup and two queued prompts never drained after "Turn completed." Didn't reproduce in a fresh dir. Reproduce or close.
ISSUE (Sab, grok pi, patched pi-acp): thinking traces now expand/collapse, but tool calls do NOT expand — tool call cards stay collapsed, no way to open their output. Repro: grok pi, run a prompt that calls bash, try expanding the tool card. Find root cause (pager tool-card expand path vs what pi-acp sends for tool_call content), fix, review, one build, READY with binary path.
ISSUE (Sab, grok claude on Air, grok-fork f1eea1fa): cannot steer a running Claude turn at all — typing while the agent works only queues the message. No keybinding to 'send queued message now as a steer' (Claude Code has this; native Grok Build likely has one too). Sab: "I cannot steer at all, I can only queue messages". Find how the native grok agent path steers mid-turn (keybinding + what it sends) and how the external ACP path (claude-acp, pi-acp) differs; ACP supports session/prompt while a turn is in flight for claude-code-acp (it interrupts/steers). Implement steer-now for external agents with the same keybinding native uses; review, one build on the VM is fine for tests but ship = gb-build sab-mini; log READY with the keybinding Sab should press.
FOLLOW-UP (low priority, Sab): steer currently cancels the in-flight turn. Sab expected insertion after the current tool call, not interrupt. Where the adapter allows it (check claude-acp / pi-acp for a safe concurrent prompt or a queued-user-message path), make steer inject at the next tool-call boundary and only fall back to cancel-and-send when it can't. Keep double-Enter as the gesture.
ISSUE (Sab, grok claude): auth-error rewrite — Grok turns Claude's 'Not logged in · Please run /login' into 'Authentication required. Try sending again.' Show the agent's real message. Low priority, after T2.
T3-SUBAGENTS (Sab, top priority, run concurrently with T1/T2 on its own cursor-agent grok-4.7 worker): Sab: "The biggest thing holding back from parity with claude code is the fact that Grok Claude cannot reliably make subagents as observable or steerable as claude code can". Facts (scout, verified in source): adapter is @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp 0.76.0 at ~/.local/share/zed/external_agents/registry/npx/claude-acp/node_modules/@agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp/dist/. tools.js:19-34 maps Task/Agent to one tool_call kind=think; native-subagents.js (~248) instead emits subagent_spawned {subagentSessionId,name,task} and tags child updates with _meta.claudeCode.parentToolUseId, but ONLY if the client advertises capabilities.subagents / nativeSubagentSessions (acp-subagents.js:3-9, air-extension.js:1). Pager initialize (xai-grok-pager/src/acp/mod.rs:458-481 client_capabilities_meta) advertises neither. Dashboard is fed by handle_ext_notification (app/acp_handler/mod.rs:658) -> classify_subagent_lifecycle (subagent_lifecycle.rs:105) from XaiSessionUpdate::SubagentSpawned/Progress/Finished {subagent_id, child_session_id, subagent_type, description} into AgentView.subagent_sessions (agent_view/mod.rs:1392). Deliver: (1) advertise the capability for external claude agents; (2) translate adapter subagent_spawned + parentToolUseId-tagged updates + completion into the Grok lifecycle events so Claude subagents show in /dashboard and as child views with streaming tool calls, same as native; (3) STEERABLE: find how the adapter accepts a prompt to a child session (session/prompt with subagentSessionId? check native-subagents.js) and wire the pager's existing steer-a-subagent path to it, so Sab can select a Claude subagent and send it a message / cancel it; (4) same translation for pi-acp if pi-subagents emit anything over ACP, else note the gap in OBSERVATIONS.md. Review, one VM debug build for tests, then ship via gb-build sab-mini; READY with the keys Sab presses to open the dashboard and steer a child.
T3-SUBAGENTS addendum (Sab, Zed + claude-agent-acp, 2026-10-13): "Claude had dispatched sub-agents ... As the agents returned their results, the TUI seemingly broke so that nothing was streaming anymore. And I would send a reply, nothing would happen, and then I would just somehow get updated to Claude responding to my reply, and everything in between was skipped." Claude itself then said "Your message came through twice, probably because of the TUI trouble". Likely cause: background Task agents complete between prompt turns; ACP session/update only flows inside a session/prompt turn, so the adapter has no turn to stream the completion notices or Claude's follow-up into, and replays queued input. Required: (a) reproduce in grok claude with claude-agent-acp 0.76: dispatch 2+ background subagents, go idle, let them finish; (b) make their completion and Claude's reaction stream live (adapter may need an idle-turn / unsolicited update path, or the pager must open a turn when the adapter signals pending output), (c) no duplicate delivery of the user's next message. Add to OBSERVATIONS.md with the adapter version.
