T1 substrate update (orchestrator, 10:48Z): read ~/.dsh/briefs/pi-durable-2026-10-13.md. Pi 1.0 shipped (pkg now @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent, latest 1.2.0; VM has 0.87.1). Pi Durable (@earendil-works/pi-durable) is single-process-owned, no cross-process resume, no human-wait primitive -> not usable for the decision packet yet; note it as migration target. pi-durable-subagents (purboo, v1.0.39, needs pi 1.0.x) has an outside-process CLI: run / send --kind answer|steer|follow-up / describe / events / stop, onQuit=pause, resume continues same sessions -> that is the resume handle for the decision packet. Fold into T1: the slice's workflow runs on pi-durable-subagents under a PINNED pi 1.0.4 installed in a scratch prefix (e.g. ~/.local/pi-1.0.4, npm i -g --prefix; do NOT replace ~/.local/bin/pi 0.87.1 which grok pi and the other workers use), and the Fable decider acts through that CLI. Unless the proposer shows a concrete reason the two community workflow packages do it better. 1.2.0 breaks our extensions (before_agent_start, sendUserMessage deliverAs) so stay at 1.0.4/1.1.0.
